PegResponsiveIrm::setCurveConfig(CurveConfig)
├── given caller is not the current owner
│   ├── when caller is a non-owner or the pending owner has not accepted ownership
│   │   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller)
│   ├── it should prioritize authorization over configuration validation and checkpointing
│   ├── it should leave curveConfig and the complete IRState unchanged
│   └── it should not call the market or emit events
└── given caller is the current owner
    ├── given the price configuration is invalid
    │   ├── when stressPrice is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
    │   ├── when recoveryPrice is greater than MAX_RECOVERY_PRICE
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
    │   ├── when stressPrice equals recoveryPrice
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
    │   └── when stressPrice is greater than recoveryPrice
    │       └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
    ├── given the price configuration is valid and the rate configuration is invalid
    │   ├── when baseRate is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
    │   ├── when baseRate is greater than stressRate
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
    │   ├── when stressRate equals maxRate
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
    │   ├── when stressRate is greater than maxRate
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
    │   └── when maxRate is greater than MAX_BORROW_RATE
    │       └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
    ├── given the price and rate configuration are valid and the controller configuration is invalid
    │   ├── when doublingDistance is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidControllerConfig
    │   ├── when recoveryDelay is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidControllerConfig
    │   └── when maxOracleAge is zero
    │       └── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidControllerConfig
    ├── given more than one configuration group is invalid
    │   ├── when the price group is invalid
    │   │   └── it should prioritize PegResponsiveIrmInvalidPriceConfig
    │   └── when the price group is valid and both rate and controller groups are invalid
    │       └── it should prioritize PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
    ├── given any configuration input is structurally invalid
    │   ├── it should reject before querying or checkpointing the market
    │   ├── it should leave curveConfig and the complete IRState unchanged
    │   └── it should not emit events
    └── given the new configuration passes structural validation
        ├── when stressPrice is one and recoveryPrice is two
        │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero ordered price thresholds subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when stressPrice equals recoveryPrice minus one
        │   └── it should accept the immediate valid side of the strict price ordering subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when recoveryPrice equals MAX_RECOVERY_PRICE
        │   └── it should accept the exact supported price ceiling subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when baseRate is one
        │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero base rate subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when baseRate equals stressRate
        │   └── it should accept the inclusive rate boundary subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when maxRate equals stressRate plus one
        │   └── it should accept the immediate valid side of the strict rate ordering subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when maxRate equals MAX_BORROW_RATE
        │   └── it should accept the exact rate ceiling subject to the post-checkpoint rate check
        ├── when doublingDistance is one
        │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero doubling distance subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when recoveryDelay is one
        │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero recovery delay subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when maxOracleAge is one
        │   └── it should accept the minimum non-zero oracle age subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when doublingDistance is type(uint256).max
        │   └── it should accept the unbounded upper distance subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when recoveryDelay is type(uint48).max
        │   └── it should accept the maximum stored delay subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when maxOracleAge is type(uint48).max
        │   └── it should accept the maximum stored age subject to the post-checkpoint rate ceiling
        ├── when maxOracleAge is less than recoveryDelay
        │   └── it should not enforce a relationship between those fields
        ├── when maxOracleAge equals recoveryDelay
        │   └── it should not enforce a relationship between those fields
        ├── when maxOracleAge is greater than recoveryDelay
        │   └── it should not enforce a relationship between those fields
        ├── given market is not set
        │   ├── it should skip the market paused query
        │   └── it should skip market accrual
        ├── given market is set
        │   ├── it should query paused with the exact PAUSE_TYPE
        │   ├── when the paused query reverts or its return data cannot be decoded
        │   │   ├── it should bubble the failure
        │   │   ├── it should leave curveConfig and IRState unchanged
        │   │   └── it should not emit setter events
        │   ├── when paused returns true
        │   │   └── it should skip accrueInterest
        │   └── when paused returns false
        │       ├── when accrueInterest reverts
        │       │   ├── it should bubble the market revert
        │       │   ├── it should atomically roll back market and IRM effects
        │       │   └── it should not emit setter events
        │       └── when accrueInterest succeeds
        │           ├── it should call market.accrueInterest exactly once
        │           ├── if the market calls back into this IRM, that callback should observe the old oracle and old curveConfig
        │           └── it should use any callback-driven post-checkpoint IRState for subsequent checks
        ├── given the post-checkpoint borrowRate is greater than newConfig.maxRate
        │   ├── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidRateConfig
        │   ├── it should roll back the nested checkpoint and all setter effects atomically
        │   └── it should not emit surviving events
        ├── given the pre-checkpoint borrowRate is at most newConfig.maxRate but the checkpoint raises it above the new maximum
        │   └── it should reject using the post-checkpoint rate
        ├── given the pre-checkpoint borrowRate is above newConfig.maxRate but the checkpoint lowers it to the new maximum or below
        │   └── it should accept using the post-checkpoint rate
        ├── given the post-checkpoint borrowRate equals newConfig.maxRate
        │   └── it should accept the exact ceiling boundary
        └── given the post-checkpoint borrowRate is at most newConfig.maxRate
            ├── when newConfig equals the stored configuration
            │   ├── it should still perform the applicable checkpoint
            │   └── it should accept and emit the replacement event
            ├── when the stored rate is below newConfig.baseRate or newConfig.stressRate
            │   ├── it should accept the configuration because only the maximum is checked
            │   └── it should not immediately derive a rate from the new configuration
            ├── it should store every newConfig field exactly
            ├── it should not re-evaluate stressMode against the new thresholds
            ├── given post-checkpoint recoveryStartedAt is zero
            │   ├── it should preserve the complete post-checkpoint IRState
            │   ├── it should emit exactly SetCurveConfig(newConfig) among setter events
            │   └── it should not emit an additional StressStateUpdated or IRStateUpdated for recovery reset
            └── given post-checkpoint recoveryStartedAt is non-zero
                ├── it should clear recoveryStartedAt
                ├── it should preserve post-checkpoint borrowRate, lastUpdate and stressMode
                ├── it should emit StressStateUpdated(stressMode, 0, 0)
                ├── it should then emit IRStateUpdated with the resulting state
                └── it should then emit SetCurveConfig(newConfig)
